  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nMixed pre-market action with SPY sitting near flat at $739.29 while tech gets hammered down 0.98%. VIX dropping to 27.59 suggests some risk appetite returning, but that elevated level still screams caution. Classic Monday indecision with geopolitical noise from Iran-Pakistan developments creating cross-currents.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fed Venable Speech (12:30 ET)</strong> - Any hawkish tilt could crush this fragile bounce</li>\n<li><strong>NY Fed Services Activity Index (12:30 ET)</strong> - Services strength critical for soft landing narrative</li>\n<li><strong>NAHB Housing Market Index (14:00 ET)</strong> - Real estate leading pre-market, watch for confirmation</li>\n<li><strong>Treasury Auctions (15:30 ET)</strong> - 3M/6M bills with \"ominous bond trades\" headlines circulating</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nDefensive rotation in full swing with staples (+1.24%) and financials (+1.06%) leading while tech bleeds. Real estate matching financials suggests rate cut expectations building despite bond market warnings. Classic flight from growth to value when geopolitical uncertainty spikes.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Iran war developments dominating flow - Pakistan deploying jets to Saudi Arabia while peace proposals circulate. Markets hate uncertainty more than bad news.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Bond market screaming higher rates ahead while equity markets pricing cuts. This disconnect ends badly - usually with equities catching down to bonds.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>BOE pause signals from IMF suggest central bank pivot accelerating globally. VIX decline indicates professional money stepping back in selectively.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY $735</strong> - Key support from Friday's low, break targets $728</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ $700</strong> - Psychological support with tech under pressure</li>\n<li><strong>VIX $30</strong> - Resistance level that's capped rallies all month</li>\n<li><strong>XLF $45.50</strong> - Financials testing breakout level on rate expectations</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>"
